  {
   "id": "ovuTiWkXBQAJ",
   "from": "Zhian Kamvar",
   "author": "d192ec4b1d416345",
   "date": "2020-01-02T09:39:47Z",
   "subject": "Re: [poppr] Bootstrapping genclone ploidy=4",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>At the moment, no, it&#39;s not possible to use aboot to bootstrap the collapsed matrix. Part of the reason for this is because the bootstrap assumes that the samples in the matrix stay constant so it can figure out the node values for the tree. Collapsing samples by MLL violates this because you would need to do it for every bootstrap iteration, resulting in different subsets of samples being collapsed. <br><br></div><div>Hope that helps.</div><div><br></div><div>Best,</div><div>Zhian<br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Mon, Dec 23, 2019 at 5:57 AM <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">walter...@ufz.de</a> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">walter...@ufz.de</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
